caption: Armor and Survivability — Overview
technology-rule: overview

Use covert, anatomical, chassis, and vehicle scales consistently. Local armor protects only its location.

Local DR protects only its location. Hardened is appropriate when armor is designed to resist armor divisors. Reserve dDR for genuinely vehicle-scale bodies.

| TL | Class I - Covert Armor | Class II - Anatomical Armor | Class III - Chassis Armor |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| TL8 | DR 1-2 | DR 5-15 | DR 20-40 bulky prototype |
| TL9 | DR 4 general or DR 12 vs cutting/piercing | Up to DR 50/30 | DR 70/50 to DR 200/120 |
| TL10 | DR 6 general or DR 18 vs cutting/piercing | Up to DR 75/45 | DR 105/75 to DR 150/100+ |
| TL11 | DR 8-12 general or DR 24-36 narrow | Up to DR 100/60 | DR 200/150+ |
| TL12 | DR 20 living metal; DR 30 energy weave; DR 50 if effectively an integrated suit layer | Up to DR 150/90 | DR 300+, vehicle DR, or dDR |

| Armor Source | Typical Hardened Access |
| --- | --- |
| TL8 ordinary cyber-plate | Usually none |
| TL9 military laminate or electromagnetic layer | Hardened 1 |
| TL10 advanced tactical shell | Hardened 1-2 |
| TL11 diamondoid, exotic matter, or nanolaminate | Hardened 2-3 |
| TL12 living metal, energy armor, or miracle laminate | Hardened 3-4 |
| Force screen | Hardened 2-5 |
| Divine or artifact armor | Hardened 1-6 |
| Superscience super-armor | Hardened 5+ with campaign approval |

| Situation | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Subdermal armor under normal clothing | Stacks normally if both cover the location. |
| Class I dermis under worn armor | Normally stacks, but the GM may enforce heat, flexibility, or medical consequences. |
| Class II integrated shell | May prevent ordinary armor; take Can't Wear Armor when appropriate. |
| Class III chassis | Uses body-specific armor modules rather than human clothing or suits. |
| Force screen | Usually stacks as a separate layer and may have Hardened or Force Field. |
| Vehicle-scale body | Use vehicle or Spaceships damage scale when the body is large enough. |

DAMAGE SCALE

Human-scale bodies use normal DR and damage. Large warbodies and mecha may use vehicle rules and dDR.
